  "plain": "A 1950s Air Force study called Special Report 14, part of Blue Book, the US Air Force's UFO study of the 1950s and 60s, is said to tell a different story in its numbers than in the press release that went out with it. A researcher on the show, whose name is not given, says that if you look at the report's own data table, something like 21 percent of almost a thousand cases were left as unknown. He credits the point to the UFO researcher Stanton Friedman, and tells it to suggest the public was given a more reassuring picture than the Air Force's own data showed."
